	System V Release 4.0		Ash Nazag

 Mac    startmac        System 7.6.1; leave with Special > Log Out
        startmac -e 8.1  Mac OS 8.1;  startmac -e 6  System 6.0.7
 TOS    starttos        EmuTOS and TeraDesk; -M TT mono, -m MB ST-RAM
        XaAES:   starttos -e xaaes  (multitasking)
        Cubase:  starttos -C $HOME/TOS/CUBASE/CUBASE31  (or SCORE, CAF)
 Amiga  startamiga      Workbench; -m MB fast RAM (or fastmb=MB in .env)
 CP/M   startcpm        Concurrent CP/M-68K; EXIT ends it, -c N joins
                        A: ~/CPM, H: home, M: temp, O: /, P: DRI's programs
 Win16  startwin        Windows for Workgroups 3.11 (Program Manager)
        Windows 3.11:  startwin -e win311
 Lisa   startlisa       Lisa Office System from ~/Lisa (lisa.rom, profile.dc42)
 V200   startvoyage200  Voyage 200 from ~/Voyage200/media; Cmd-Q quits
 NeXT   startnext       OPENSTEP 4.2 from ~/NeXT/openstep; Cmd-Q quits
 X      startx          twm; or  xsession  for a menu of sessions, or
        xsession twm|xview|mac|tos|amiga|win|lisa|voyage200|
        console|cpm

 Ctrl-Option-Command-0 shows the console, -1 to -9 the sessions.
 Ctrl-C on the console ends TOS or the Amiga.
 apkg update, apkg install NAME: packages, in /opt/amix/bin
 start* -l lists environments, -e NAME runs one, -d NAME sets the default;
 the first start makes your copy (~/System Folder, ~/TOS, ~/Amiga ...).
 -e NEW -b NAME makes a copy of NAME; -R refreshes yours from the system's.
 exit logs out; root shuts down with  shutdown -y -g0 -i0
